meta {
  name: qnib-ftest
  seq: 5
}

auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{oci_bearer}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  repo: qnib/ftest
  tag: latest
}

docs {
  # qnib-ftest — inspect the qnib/ftest artefacts populated by
  # `metahub-admin parse collections` (pullthrough-repo session).

  ## Auth prerequisite (one-time per session)

  Every request in this folder sends `Authorization: Bearer {{oci_bearer}}`
  (inherited via folder-level `auth:bearer`). To populate `oci_bearer`,
  do ONE of:

    A) Run `qnib-ftest/refreshToken` (seq 0). Single click — performs
       the /v2 WWW-Authenticate challenge AND the /auth token exchange
       inline, then stores `oci_bearer` in the active environment.
       Also honours the `profile` env var (see below).

    B) Run `auth/get` then `auth/getToken` in order (the classic path).
       Same outcome EXCEPT profile selection — classic flow always
       authenticates as plain `{{username}}` which maps to profile
       `generic`. Use `refreshToken` when you need non-generic.

  Both paths require `username` + `password` in the active environment
  (already set to `oci` / `oci` in `metahub-dev.bru` and
  `metahub-local.bru`).

  ## Picking a profile

  The collection defines `profile: generic` at the top level
  (see `collection.bru`). Profile is carried inside the Basic-auth
  username by the `<user>/<profile>` convention (see
  pkg/api/v1/handlers/auth.go and metalib's ParseProfile).
  `refreshToken` reads `profile` and builds the Basic username as
  `{{username}}/{{profile}}` unless profile == "generic".

  Precedence (lowest -> highest, Bruno standard):
    1. collection.bru (vars:pre-request { profile: generic })
    2. environments/*.bru vars
    3. folder.bru vars:pre-request
    4. per-request vars:pre-request

  To switch profile for the qnib-ftest chain, pick ONE override level:
    A) Collection-wide: edit collection.bru and change
         vars:pre-request { profile: glow#1.5.0 }
    B) Per-environment: add `profile: glow#1.5.0` to the active
       environment file (metahub-dev.bru / metahub-local.bru).
    C) Folder-wide: add `profile: glow#1.5.0` to this folder's
       vars:pre-request block below.
    D) Per-request: add `vars:pre-request { profile: glow#1.5.0 }`
       to a single .bru file.

  Common labels:
    profile: generic             (the default, always works)
    profile: glow#1.5.0          (wraps manifests with the glow layer)
    profile: cpu#zen2            (microarch variant)

  Then re-run `refreshToken` to mint a new `oci_bearer` for that
  profile, and run the rest of the chain. The server resolves a
  DIFFERENT `:Index` per profile, so the Index body / child
  manifests / layer digests will differ.

  Example: for `profile: generic` the Index has 1 child (arm64,
  size 735). For `profile: glow#1.5.0` the Index has 2 children
  (arm64 + amd64 with the glow layer applied, each size 1056).

  ## Request sequence

  After `refreshToken` (seq 0) runs, execute the inspection chain in
  order — each post-response script extracts the variable the next
  step needs:

    0. refreshToken        — mint oci_bearer (single-click auth)
    1. getTagsList         — confirm the Tag is discoverable
    2. headIndexByTag      — HEAD the Slot's computed :Index,
                             content-negotiated as an OCI image-index
                             (regression guard #10)
    3. getIndexByTag       — GET body; post-script extracts
                             `indexDigest` + `childManifestDigest` +
                             `childManifestSize`
    4. getIndexByDigest    — round-trip Index by its own digest
    5. headChildManifest   — HEAD first per-arch manifest; cross-checks
                             Index-descriptor-size vs manifest-body-size
                             (regression guard for metalib aefa27f)
    6. getChildManifest    — GET same; extracts `configDigest` +
                             `firstLayerDigest`
    7. getConfigBlob       — GET image config blob (regression guard
                             for pipeline-repo cab4cf7 bucket alignment)
    8. headLayerBlob       — HEAD first layer blob
    9. neo4jSlotChain      — out-of-band Neo4j Cypher: Slot->HAS_PUSHED
                             ->Manifest + Slot->POINTS_TO->Index counts
                             (mirrors Verify-CE #9)

  The chain mirrors what `manifest-tool inspect <registry>/qnib/ftest:latest`
  performs under the hood. Each step's post-response script raises a
  contextual error if it fails, so "step 4 returned 404" isolates the
  problem immediately.
}
